# SpatiA11y – Spatial Audio Accessibility Prototype

This project explores spatial audio interfaces for accessibility using Apple's PHASE framework. It enables users to navigate and interact with virtual "widgets" through spatialized sound and touch-based exploration.

## Concept

The system maps UI elements (widgets) into a 3D audio space. Users:
- Drag their finger to explore space
- Hear spatialized sounds tied to objects
- Tap to trigger text-to-speech (TTS)
- Adjust audio properties via a control panel

This builds toward an **"ear-in-hand" interaction paradigm** for non-visual navigation.

---

## Architecture Overview

### Core Systems

- PHASEManager – Handles audio engine setup, listener, and spatial audio pipeline :contentReference[oaicite:0]{index=0}  
- WidgetAudioGrid – Manages spatial layout of widgets, sound playback, and TTS :contentReference[oaicite:1]{index=1}  
- SpatialAudioManager – Applies UI settings to audio system :contentReference[oaicite:2]{index=2}  
- HeadTrackingManager – Tracks head orientation via AirPods motion sensors :contentReference[oaicite:3]{index=3}  

### UI Layers

- InterfaceView – Main exploration interface (drag + tap interactions) :contentReference[oaicite:4]{index=4}  
- ControlPanelView – Adjust widget/global audio settings :contentReference[oaicite:5]{index=5}  
- MainContainerView – Switches between interface and control panel :contentReference[oaicite:6]{index=6}  

### Data + Config

- AudioAssetLibrary – Available sounds categorized (nature, pads, etc.) :contentReference[oaicite:7]{index=7}  
- WidgetAudioSettings / GlobalAudioSettings** – State models for audio parameters :contentReference[oaicite:8]{index=8} :contentReference[oaicite:9]{index=9}  

---

## Features

- Spatialized looping audio per widget
- Touch-based exploration (audio starts/stops on touch)
- TTS labeling of nearby objects
- Head tracking support (AirPods)
- Adjustable:
  - Volume
  - Pitch
  - Spread
  - Distance gain
  - Reverb
- Dynamic sound switching per widget

---

